cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Semantic Coherence and Transformer Architectures for Zero-Day Wordlist DGA Detection
message: >-
  If you use this benchmark, code, or findings in your work, please cite it
  using this metadata.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Walid
    family-names: Mahmood
    affiliation: Department of Computer Science and Engineering, BRAC University
identifier: https://github.com/WalidMahmood/dga-detection-generalization
repository-code: https://github.com/WalidMahmood/dga-detection-generalization
abstract: >-
  A leak-free Leave-Families-Out benchmark for zero-day wordlist-based Domain
  Generation Algorithm (DGA) detection on 1.3M domains spanning 43 DGA
  families. Seven systems are compared, including two proposed dual-branch
  architectures (Dual-Branch v3, 4.10M parameters; Dual-Branch Coherent, 0.73M
  parameters, with an explicit 6-dimensional FastText pairwise-cosine coherence
  vector), a fine-tuned ModernBERT-Base (149M), and two soft-voting ensembles.
  Under fully blind conditions the 0.73M coherence model outperforms the 149M
  transformer on the hardest unseparated dictionary family (matsnu, +24.4%
  relative recall with 204x fewer parameters), while the transformer dominates
  aggregate F1 and benign specificity.
keywords:
  - DGA detection
  - domain generation algorithms
  - wordlist DGA
  - zero-day generalization
  - semantic coherence
  - FastText
  - ModernBERT
  - BiLSTM
  - DNS security
  - machine learning security
